.TH YAZI 1 "2026-06-19" "yazi 26.5.6" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yazi \- terminal file manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yazi
.RI [ directory ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yazi
is a fast terminal file manager written in Rust with a focus on
asynchronous I/O performance.
It provides a three-pane Miller-column layout, file previews
(including images, archives, and documents via adapters),
and a plugin system for extensibility.
.PP
An optional
.I directory
argument opens yazi in that path instead of the current directory.
.PP
This package is a repack of the upstream pre-built musl binary release.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.BR h " / " j " / " k " / " l
Navigate (parent / down / up / enter directory)
.TP
.BR Enter
Open file with default application
.TP
.BR Space
Toggle selection
.TP
.BR y
Yank (copy) selected files
.TP
.BR d
Cut selected files
.TP
.BR p
Paste
.TP
.BR D
Delete to trash
.TP
.BR /
Search by name
.TP
.BR q
Quit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ya (1),
.PP
Full documentation at
.IR https://yazi-rs.github.io .
